ill in those  statements or a suggestion of that by  Jared Kushner the president's senior  advisor and his son-in-law saying in  fact this would have to be a joint  american-israeli decision but now it  appears we have some clarity coming from  the US Secretary of State saying that in  fact this is an Israeli decision and it  doesn't appear that he is suggesting  that there should be any positive any  sort anymore all right let's thank  Kimberly halket more to discuss on this  though we head over to Harry Fawcett in  West Jerusalem we had any reaction out  of the Israeli government of course we  should say the new Israeli government  yes not yet and I think that is key that  there is this new Israeli government as  of Monday evening the unity emergency  government as they're calling it in  which been against the former leader of  the opposition joined Benjamin Netanyahu  allowing him to stay in office he said  because of the current emergency with  coronavirus but as part of the  negotiations which led up to that  announcement he gave way on a what had  been a key issue being the annexation of  large parts of the occupied West Bank it  had been understood that he was seeking  a veto trying to ensure that other  voices were brought into the picture  before any move was made on annexation  including Israel's neighbors in the  region and also European nations but  that is not there in the deal that was  announced indeed it says from July the  first Benjamin Netanyahu can bring it  both the cabinet and to the Israeli  Parliament the Knesset and so that  combined with the fact that there is  this signal from the United States from  this very senior US government figure in  Mike Pompeo does suggest that things are  moving in that direction there is  supposed to be still this mapping plan  the the a joint team of US and Israeli  officials delineating exactly which  parts under the plan that was announced  in January  could be annexed by Israel but it seems  pretty clear that as far as Mike Pompeo  is concerned the ultimate decision will  be up to Israel alright let's cross our  thank Harry we're gonna join now on the  day Brahim  from Ramallah in the occupied West Bank  and nadare I imagine this is only going  to further cement the Palestinians  suspicions of the u.s. not really  playing that role as an honest broker  yes and they've been saying that ever  since the US administration announced  plans to move its embassy from Tel Aviv  to Jerusalem Palestinians have been  saying that the u.s. lost its  credibility as an honest broker for the  peace process they've been calling for  an international peace conference where  different parties play a role in ending  that conflict now to the issue of the  statement of Pompeo we've spoken to the  member of the executive committee of the  PLO Hanan Ashrawi she says that these  statements not only encourage Israel to  continue its actions on the ground but  gives it the cover to annex and steal  more lands we've heard also from the  Palestinian president spokesperson Nabil  aboard Ana who says that this only  empowers Israel but also that the u.s.  does not really have any legitimacy or  any ownership of the land to give Israel  the legitimacy to an exit the  Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas have  been addressing the nation in a  televised pre-recorded televised speech  that was recorded before their Pompeo  statement but he addressed this very  issue and it's expected that his  position will remain the same the same  even after he said that he will be  cutting all signed agreements with  Israel if Israel most forward with these  plans of course this is a statement that  we've heard from Abbas many times and  many analysts would say that he really  doesn't have any more cards to play at  this point that's why he's been seeking  the international community it's been  saying that this is illegal under  international law and Israel now is more  empowered than ever by the current US  administration to continue with its  actions on the ground including  annexation which is considered illegal  under international law all right  Ibrahim from Ramallah
 

